  "term": "spontaneous movement",
  "definition": "In this context, spontaneous movement refers to natural, unforced movement emphasized within a relaxation method used to help manage stress, pain, and blood pressure. It is presented as part of a broader practice that also uses concentration, objective attention to visual and auditory experiences, controlled self-awareness, and responsiveness in relationships.",
